1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,033
On vacation, you're a different person. You wake up early. You barely touch your phone. Then you get home, and the old you is waiting.

2
00:00:08,139 --> 00:00:14,167
You try harder. It works, for a few days. Then one night, you're scrolling in bed without deciding to.

3
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:22,100
It feels like weak willpower. But a strong habit doesn't wait for permission. Its cues can set it off, whatever you intend.

4
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:31,100
When researchers followed students who moved to a new university, their old habits fell apart, except where parts of the old setting stayed the same.

5
00:00:31,187 --> 00:00:37,033
Psychologists call this habit discontinuity. New cues open a window to choose again.

6
00:00:37,142 --> 00:00:41,367
So tonight, try an experiment: charge your phone outside the bedroom.

7
00:00:41,453 --> 00:00:45,567
You can't always out-will a cue. But you can choose where it lives.

8
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:48,400
Follow The Psychology of Becoming.
